# Steady heat conduction through a bar of two materials in series with
# L1 = L2 = 1 and k1 = 50, k2 = 10, held at T = 0 at the bottom and T = 100 at
# the top. The cards of each material are written in an order other than
# *DENSITY, *SPECIFIC HEAT, *CONDUCTIVITY, and one card has a temperature
# column. The interface at z = 1 is at T = 100*k2/(k1 + k2) = 16.667.
!VERSION
 3
!SOLUTION, TYPE=HEAT
!FIXTEMP
 BOTTOM, 0.0
 TOP, 100.0
!SOLVER, METHOD=CG, PRECOND=1, ITERLOG=NO, TIMELOG=NO
 10000, 1
 1.0e-10, 1.0, 0.0
!WRITE, RESULT
!END
